<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBProperty
      Source: StGB consolidated, property and economic offences (provenance StGB 242, 246, 248b, 248c, 249, 253, 257, 258, 259, 261, 263, 263a, 303, 303a, 303b, 305; German governs)
      One combined carrier for sixteen sections spanning the Nineteenth to Twenty-seventh Titles (theft; robbery and
      extortion; assistance, obstruction, handling and laundering; fraud; criminal damage). Each section is a
      SectionScope; identifiers resolve within their SectionScope. The same token (for example ForSelf, KeepsInCustody,
      Destroys, Alters, Unlawfully) may carry a section-specific surface form: each section's variables are declared
      in that section's own groups, exactly as emitted by the per-section build, and the per-section schemas remain
      the canonical single-section substrates. Cross-scope identities resolve by name: the 259 scope's Stolen against
      the 242 scope; the 303b scope's CommitsDataAlteration against the 303a scope; the 303a and 303b preparation
      rules against the Section 202c scope of the data-cluster carrier. The 263a, 303a and 303b scopes are the
      contract rebuilds of 10 June 2026, superseding the 7 June data-cluster versions of those sections. Objective
      Tatbestand only; intent, purpose and knowledge elements retained where the markup retains them; penalties
      excluded; silent repairs against the German recorded in the Flags annexes of the working document, not here.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Property and Economic Offences (§242 to §305)</Subject><Verb>commit</Verb><Article>StGB 242, 246, 248b, 248c, 249, 253, 257, 258, 259, 261, 263, 263a, 303, 303a, 303b, 305</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBProperty</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

